==English==
{{was wotd|2009|March|26}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|conterminous}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|conterminus}}, from {{m|la|con-||with}} + {{m|la|terminus||border, end}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/kəˈtəː.mɪ.nəs/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/kəˈtɝ.mɪ.nəs/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Meeting [[end-to-end|end to end]] or at the ends.
# {{lb|en|geography}} Having matching boundaries; or, [[adjoin|adjoining]] and sharing a [[boundary]].
#: ''New York's borough of Brooklyn and Kings County are '''conterminous'''.''
#: ''To get a building warrant he had to show the plans to "'''conterminous''' proprietors", neighbours with whom his property shared a boundary.''
# Having the same [[scope]], [[range]] of meaning, or [[extent]] in time.
# {{lb|en|legal}} Said of linked or related property leases that expire together.

